id: basic-concepts
title: Basic Concepts and Terminology
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page introduces the basic concepts and terminology used in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-form"},{"type":"text","value":" library. Familiarizing yourself with these concepts will help you better understand and work with the library."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"form-instance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form Instance"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Form Instance is an object that represents an individual form and provides methods and properties for working with the form. You create a form instance using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectForm"},{"type":"text","value":" function. The hook accepts an object with an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" function, which is called when the form is submitted."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const form = injectForm({\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n    // Do something with form data\n    console.log(value)\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"field","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Field represents a single form input element, such as a text input or a checkbox. Fields are created using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstackField"},{"type":"text","value":" directive. The directive accepts a name prop, which should match a key in the form's default values. It also exposes a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field"},{"type":"text","value":" named instance of the directive's internals that should be used via a template variable to access the field's internals."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"firstName\" #firstName=\"field\">\n  <input\n    [value]=\"firstName.api.state.value\"\n    (blur)=\"firstName.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (input)=\"firstName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n  />\n</ng-container>","lang":"html"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"field-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each field has its own state, which includes its current value, validation status, error messages, and other metadata. You can access a field's state using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fieldApi.state"},{"type":"text","value":" property."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const {\n  value,\n  meta: { errors, isValidating },\n} = field.state","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are four states in the metadata that can be useful to see how the user interacts with a field:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"isTouched\""}]},{"type":"text","value":", after the user changes the field or blurs the field"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"isDirty\""}]},{"type":"text","value":", after the field's value has been changed, even if it's been reverted to the default. Opposite of "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"isPristine\""}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"isPristine\""}]},{"type":"text","value":", until the user changes the field value. Opposite of "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"isDirty\""}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"isBlurred\""}]},{"type":"text","value":", after the field has been blurred"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const { isTouched, isDirty, isPristine, isBlurred } = field.state.meta","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"image","src":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/field-states.png","alt":"Field states"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"understanding-isdirty-in-different-libraries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Understanding 'isDirty' in Different Libraries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Non-Persistent "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dirty"},{"type":"text","value":" state"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Libraries"}]},{"type":"text","value":": React Hook Form (RHF), Formik, Final Form."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]},{"type":"text","value":": A field is 'dirty' if its value differs from the default. Reverting to the default value makes it 'clean' again."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistent "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dirty"},{"type":"text","value":" state"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Libraries"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Angular Form, Vue FormKit."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]},{"type":"text","value":": A field remains 'dirty' once changed, even if reverted to the default value."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We have chosen the persistent 'dirty' state model. To also support a non-persistent 'dirty' state, we introduce an additional flag:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"isDefaultValue\""}]},{"type":"text","value":", whether the field's current value is the default value"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const { isDefaultValue, isTouched } = field.state.meta\n\n// The following line will re-create the non-Persistent `dirty` functionality.\nconst nonPersistentIsDirty = !isDefaultValue","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"image","src":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/field-states-extended.png","alt":"Field states extended"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"field-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Field API is an object accessed in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstackField.api"},{"type":"text","value":" property when creating a field. It provides methods for working with the field's state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<input\n  [value]=\"fieldName.api.state.value\"\n  (blur)=\"fieldName.api.handleBlur()\"\n  (input)=\"fieldName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n/>","lang":"angular-html"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-form"},{"type":"text","value":" provides both synchronous and asynchronous validation out of the box. Validation functions can be passed to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstackField"},{"type":"text","value":" directive using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators"},{"type":"text","value":" prop."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"firstName\" #firstName=\"field\">\n      <input\n        [value]=\"firstName.api.state.value\"\n        (blur)=\"firstName.api.handleBlur()\"\n        (input)=\"firstName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n      />\n    </ng-container>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  firstNameValidator: FieldValidateFn<any, any, string, any> = ({ value }) =>\n    !value\n      ? 'A first name is required'\n      : value.length < 3\n        ? 'First name must be at least 3 characters'\n        : undefined\n\n  firstNameAsyncValidator: FieldValidateAsyncFn<any, string, any> = async ({\n    value,\n  }) => {\n    await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000))\n    return value.includes('error') && 'No \"error\" allowed in first name'\n  }\n\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n}","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validation-with-standard-schema-libraries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation with Standard Schema Libraries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In addition to hand-rolled validation options, we also support the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/standard-schema/standard-schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard Schema"}]},{"type":"text","value":" specification."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can define a schema using any of the libraries implementing the specification and pass it to a form or field validator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported libraries include:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://zod.dev/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Zod"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (v3.24.0 or higher)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://valibot.dev/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Valibot"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (v1.0.0 or higher)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://arktype.io/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ArkType"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (v2.1.20 or higher)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/jquense/yup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (v1.7.0 or higher)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { z } from 'zod'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container\n      [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n      name=\"firstName\"\n      [validators]=\"{\n        onChange: z.string().min(3, 'First name must be at least 3 characters'),\n        onChangeAsyncDebounceMs: 500,\n        onChangeAsync: firstNameAsyncValidator,\n      }\"\n      #firstName=\"field\"\n    >\n      <!-- ... -->\n    </ng-container>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  firstNameAsyncValidator = z.string().refine(\n    async (value) => {\n      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000))\n      return !value.includes('error')\n    },\n    {\n      message: \"No 'error' allowed in first name\",\n    },\n  )\n\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n\n  z = z\n}","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reactivity","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactivity"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-form"},{"type":"text","value":" offers a way to subscribe to form and field state changes via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectStore(this.form, selector)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { injectForm, injectStore } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component(/*...*/)\nclass AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm(/*...*/)\n  canSubmit = injectStore(this.form, (state) => state.canSubmit)\n  isSubmitting = injectStore(this.form, (state) => state.isSubmitting)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"listeners","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Listeners"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-form"},{"type":"text","value":" allows you to react to specific triggers and \"listen\" to them to dispatch side effects."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container\n      [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n      name=\"country\"\n      [listeners]=\"{\n        onChange: onCountryChange\n      }\"\n      #country=\"field\"\n    ></ng-container>\n  `,\n})\n\n...\n\nonCountryChange: FieldListenerFn<any, any, any, any, string> = ({\n    value,\n  }) => {\n    console.log(`Country changed to: ${value}, resetting province`)\n    this.form.setFieldValue('province', '')\n  }","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"More information can be found at "},{"type":"link","href":"./listeners.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Listeners"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"array-fields","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array Fields"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array fields allow you to manage a list of values within a form, such as a list of hobbies. You can create an array field using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstackField"},{"type":"text","value":" directive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When working with array fields, you can use the fields "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pushValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"removeValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"swapValues"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"moveValue"},{"type":"text","value":" methods to add, remove, swap, and move a value from one index to another within the array, respectively. Additional helper methods such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"insertValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"replaceValue"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clearValues"},{"type":"text","value":" are also available for inserting, replacing, and clearing array values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"hobbies\" #hobbies=\"field\">\n      <div>\n        Hobbies\n        <div>\n          @if (!hobbies.api.state.value.length) {\n            No hobbies found\n          }\n          @for (_ of hobbies.api.state.value; track $index) {\n            <div>\n              <ng-container\n                [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n                [name]=\"getHobbyName($index)\"\n                #hobbyName=\"field\"\n              >\n                <div>\n                  <label [for]=\"hobbyName.api.name\">Name:</label>\n                  <input\n                    [id]=\"hobbyName.api.name\"\n                    [name]=\"hobbyName.api.name\"\n                    [value]=\"hobbyName.api.state.value\"\n                    (blur)=\"hobbyName.api.handleBlur()\"\n                    (input)=\"\n                      hobbyName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\n                    \"\n                  />\n                  <button\n                    type=\"button\"\n                    (click)=\"hobbies.api.removeValue($index)\"\n                  >\n                    X\n                  </button>\n                </div>\n              </ng-container>\n              <ng-container\n                [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n                [name]=\"getHobbyDesc($index)\"\n                #hobbyDesc=\"field\"\n              >\n                <div>\n                  <label [for]=\"hobbyDesc.api.name\">Description:</label>\n                  <input\n                    [id]=\"hobbyDesc.api.name\"\n                    [name]=\"hobbyDesc.api.name\"\n                    [value]=\"hobbyDesc.api.state.value\"\n                    (blur)=\"hobbyDesc.api.handleBlur()\"\n                    (input)=\"\n                      hobbyDesc.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\n                    \"\n                  />\n                </div>\n              </ng-container>\n            </div>\n          }\n        </div>\n        <button type=\"button\" (click)=\"hobbies.api.pushValue(defaultHobby)\">\n          Add hobby\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    </ng-container>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  defaultHobby = {\n    name: '',\n    description: '',\n    yearsOfExperience: 0,\n  }\n\n  getHobbyName = (idx: number) => `hobbies[${idx}].name` as const\n  getHobbyDesc = (idx: number) => `hobbies[${idx}].description` as const\n\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      hobbies: [] as Array<{\n        name: string\n        description: string\n        yearsOfExperience: number\n      }>,\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      alert(JSON.stringify(value))\n    },\n  })\n}","lang":"angular-ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These are the basic concepts and terminology used in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-form"},{"type":"text","value":" library. Understanding these concepts will help you work more effectively with the library and create complex forms with ease."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"form-instance","text":"Form Instance","level":2},{"id":"field","text":"Field","level":2},{"id":"field-state","text":"Field State","level":2},{"id":"understanding-isdirty-in-different-libraries","text":"Understanding 'isDirty' in Different Libraries","level":2},{"id":"field-api","text":"Field API","level":2},{"id":"validation","text":"Validation","level":2},{"id":"validation-with-standard-schema-libraries","text":"Validation with Standard Schema Libraries","level":2},{"id":"reactivity","text":"Reactivity","level":2},{"id":"listeners","text":"Listeners","level":2},{"id":"array-fields","text":"Array Fields","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis page introduces the basic concepts and terminology used in the `@tanstack/angular-form` library. Familiarizing yourself with these concepts will help you better understand and work with the library.\n\n## Form Instance\n\nA Form Instance is an object that represents an individual form and provides methods and properties for working with the form. You create a form instance using the `injectForm` function. The hook accepts an object with an `onSubmit` function, which is called when the form is submitted.\n\n```typescript\nconst form = injectForm({\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n    // Do something with form data\n    console.log(value)\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Field\n\nA Field represents a single form input element, such as a text input or a checkbox. Fields are created using the `tanstackField` directive. The directive accepts a name prop, which should match a key in the form's default values. It also exposes a `field` named instance of the directive's internals that should be used via a template variable to access the field's internals.\n\nExample:\n\n```html\n<ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"firstName\" #firstName=\"field\">\n  <input\n    [value]=\"firstName.api.state.value\"\n    (blur)=\"firstName.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (input)=\"firstName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n  />\n</ng-container>\n```\n\n## Field State\n\nEach field has its own state, which includes its current value, validation status, error messages, and other metadata. You can access a field's state using the `fieldApi.state` property.\n\nExample:\n\n```ts\nconst {\n  value,\n  meta: { errors, isValidating },\n} = field.state\n```\n\nThere are four states in the metadata that can be useful to see how the user interacts with a field:\n\n- _\"isTouched\"_, after the user changes the field or blurs the field\n- _\"isDirty\"_, after the field's value has been changed, even if it's been reverted to the default. Opposite of _\"isPristine\"_\n- _\"isPristine\"_, until the user changes the field value. Opposite of _\"isDirty\"_\n- _\"isBlurred\"_, after the field has been blurred\n\n```ts\nconst { isTouched, isDirty, isPristine, isBlurred } = field.state.meta\n```\n\n![Field states](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/field-states.png)\n\n## Understanding 'isDirty' in Different Libraries\n\nNon-Persistent `dirty` state\n\n- **Libraries**: React Hook Form (RHF), Formik, Final Form.\n- **Behavior**: A field is 'dirty' if its value differs from the default. Reverting to the default value makes it 'clean' again.\n\nPersistent `dirty` state\n\n- **Libraries**: Angular Form, Vue FormKit.\n- **Behavior**: A field remains 'dirty' once changed, even if reverted to the default value.\n\nWe have chosen the persistent 'dirty' state model. To also support a non-persistent 'dirty' state, we introduce an additional flag:\n\n- _\"isDefaultValue\"_, whether the field's current value is the default value\n\n```ts\nconst { isDefaultValue, isTouched } = field.state.meta\n\n// The following line will re-create the non-Persistent `dirty` functionality.\nconst nonPersistentIsDirty = !isDefaultValue\n```\n\n![Field states extended](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/field-states-extended.png)\n\n## Field API\n\nThe Field API is an object accessed in the `tanstackField.api` property when creating a field. It provides methods for working with the field's state.\n\nExample:\n\n```angular-html\n<input\n  [value]=\"fieldName.api.state.value\"\n  (blur)=\"fieldName.api.handleBlur()\"\n  (input)=\"fieldName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n/>\n```\n\n## Validation\n\n`@tanstack/angular-form` provides both synchronous and asynchronous validation out of the box. Validation functions can be passed to the `tanstackField` directive using the `validators` prop.\n\nExample:\n\n```angular-ts\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"firstName\" #firstName=\"field\">\n      <input\n        [value]=\"firstName.api.state.value\"\n        (blur)=\"firstName.api.handleBlur()\"\n        (input)=\"firstName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n      />\n    </ng-container>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  firstNameValidator: FieldValidateFn<any, any, string, any> = ({ value }) =>\n    !value\n      ? 'A first name is required'\n      : value.length < 3\n        ? 'First name must be at least 3 characters'\n        : undefined\n\n  firstNameAsyncValidator: FieldValidateAsyncFn<any, string, any> = async ({\n    value,\n  }) => {\n    await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000))\n    return value.includes('error') && 'No \"error\" allowed in first name'\n  }\n\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\n## Validation with Standard Schema Libraries\n\nIn addition to hand-rolled validation options, we also support the [Standard Schema](https://github.com/standard-schema/standard-schema) specification.\n\nYou can define a schema using any of the libraries implementing the specification and pass it to a form or field validator.\n\nSupported libraries include:\n\n- [Zod](https://zod.dev/) (v3.24.0 or higher)\n- [Valibot](https://valibot.dev/) (v1.0.0 or higher)\n- [ArkType](https://arktype.io/) (v2.1.20 or higher)\n- [Yup](https://github.com/jquense/yup) (v1.7.0 or higher)\n\nExample:\n\n```angular-ts\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container\n      [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n      name=\"firstName\"\n      [validators]=\"{\n        onChange: z.string().min(3, 'First name must be at least 3 characters'),\n        onChangeAsyncDebounceMs: 500,\n        onChangeAsync: firstNameAsyncValidator,\n      }\"\n      #firstName=\"field\"\n    >\n      <!-- ... -->\n    </ng-container>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  firstNameAsyncValidator = z.string().refine(\n    async (value) => {\n      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000))\n      return !value.includes('error')\n    },\n    {\n      message: \"No 'error' allowed in first name\",\n    },\n  )\n\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n\n  z = z\n}\n```\n\n## Reactivity\n\n`@tanstack/angular-form` offers a way to subscribe to form and field state changes via `injectStore(this.form, selector)`.\n\nExample:\n\n```typescript\nimport { injectForm, injectStore } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component(/*...*/)\nclass AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm(/*...*/)\n  canSubmit = injectStore(this.form, (state) => state.canSubmit)\n  isSubmitting = injectStore(this.form, (state) => state.isSubmitting)\n}\n```\n\n## Listeners\n\n`@tanstack/angular-form` allows you to react to specific triggers and \"listen\" to them to dispatch side effects.\n\nExample:\n\n```angular-ts\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container\n      [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n      name=\"country\"\n      [listeners]=\"{\n        onChange: onCountryChange\n      }\"\n      #country=\"field\"\n    ></ng-container>\n  `,\n})\n\n...\n\nonCountryChange: FieldListenerFn<any, any, any, any, string> = ({\n    value,\n  }) => {\n    console.log(`Country changed to: ${value}, resetting province`)\n    this.form.setFieldValue('province', '')\n  }\n```\n\nMore information can be found at [Listeners](./listeners.md)\n\n## Array Fields\n\nArray fields allow you to manage a list of values within a form, such as a list of hobbies. You can create an array field using the `tanstackField` directive.\n\nWhen working with array fields, you can use the fields `pushValue`, `removeValue`, `swapValues` and `moveValue` methods to add, remove, swap, and move a value from one index to another within the array, respectively. Additional helper methods such as `insertValue`, `replaceValue`, and `clearValues` are also available for inserting, replacing, and clearing array values.\n\nExample:\n\n```angular-ts\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"hobbies\" #hobbies=\"field\">\n      <div>\n        Hobbies\n        <div>\n          @if (!hobbies.api.state.value.length) {\n            No hobbies found\n          }\n          @for (_ of hobbies.api.state.value; track $index) {\n            <div>\n              <ng-container\n                [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n                [name]=\"getHobbyName($index)\"\n                #hobbyName=\"field\"\n              >\n                <div>\n                  <label [for]=\"hobbyName.api.name\">Name:</label>\n                  <input\n                    [id]=\"hobbyName.api.name\"\n                    [name]=\"hobbyName.api.name\"\n                    [value]=\"hobbyName.api.state.value\"\n                    (blur)=\"hobbyName.api.handleBlur()\"\n                    (input)=\"\n                      hobbyName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\n                    \"\n                  />\n                  <button\n                    type=\"button\"\n                    (click)=\"hobbies.api.removeValue($index)\"\n                  >\n                    X\n                  </button>\n                </div>\n              </ng-container>\n              <ng-container\n                [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n                [name]=\"getHobbyDesc($index)\"\n                #hobbyDesc=\"field\"\n              >\n                <div>\n                  <label [for]=\"hobbyDesc.api.name\">Description:</label>\n                  <input\n                    [id]=\"hobbyDesc.api.name\"\n                    [name]=\"hobbyDesc.api.name\"\n                    [value]=\"hobbyDesc.api.state.value\"\n                    (blur)=\"hobbyDesc.api.handleBlur()\"\n                    (input)=\"\n                      hobbyDesc.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\n                    \"\n                  />\n                </div>\n              </ng-container>\n            </div>\n          }\n        </div>\n        <button type=\"button\" (click)=\"hobbies.api.pushValue(defaultHobby)\">\n          Add hobby\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    </ng-container>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  defaultHobby = {\n    name: '',\n    description: '',\n    yearsOfExperience: 0,\n  }\n\n  getHobbyName = (idx: number) => `hobbies[${idx}].name` as const\n  getHobbyDesc = (idx: number) => `hobbies[${idx}].description` as const\n\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      hobbies: [] as Array<{\n        name: string\n        description: string\n        yearsOfExperience: number\n      }>,\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      alert(JSON.stringify(value))\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\nThese are the basic concepts and terminology used in the `@tanstack/angular-form` library. Understanding these concepts will help you work more effectively with the library and create complex forms with ease.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: basic-concepts\ntitle: Basic Concepts and Terminology\n---\n\nThis page introduces the basic concepts and terminology used in the `@tanstack/angular-form` library. Familiarizing yourself with these concepts will help you better understand and work with the library.\n\n## Form Instance\n\nA Form Instance is an object that represents an individual form and provides methods and properties for working with the form. You create a form instance using the `injectForm` function. The hook accepts an object with an `onSubmit` function, which is called when the form is submitted.\n\n```typescript\nconst form = injectForm({\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n    // Do something with form data\n    console.log(value)\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Field\n\nA Field represents a single form input element, such as a text input or a checkbox. Fields are created using the `tanstackField` directive. The directive accepts a name prop, which should match a key in the form's default values. It also exposes a `field` named instance of the directive's internals that should be used via a template variable to access the field's internals.\n\nExample:\n\n```html\n<ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"firstName\" #firstName=\"field\">\n  <input\n    [value]=\"firstName.api.state.value\"\n    (blur)=\"firstName.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (input)=\"firstName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n  />\n</ng-container>\n```\n\n## Field State\n\nEach field has its own state, which includes its current value, validation status, error messages, and other metadata. You can access a field's state using the `fieldApi.state` property.\n\nExample:\n\n```ts\nconst {\n  value,\n  meta: { errors, isValidating },\n} = field.state\n```\n\nThere are four states in the metadata that can be useful to see how the user interacts with a field:\n\n- _\"isTouched\"_, after the user changes the field or blurs the field\n- _\"isDirty\"_, after the field's value has been changed, even if it's been reverted to the default. Opposite of _\"isPristine\"_\n- _\"isPristine\"_, until the user changes the field value. Opposite of _\"isDirty\"_\n- _\"isBlurred\"_, after the field has been blurred\n\n```ts\nconst { isTouched, isDirty, isPristine, isBlurred } = field.state.meta\n```\n\n![Field states](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/field-states.png)\n\n## Understanding 'isDirty' in Different Libraries\n\nNon-Persistent `dirty` state\n\n- **Libraries**: React Hook Form (RHF), Formik, Final Form.\n- **Behavior**: A field is 'dirty' if its value differs from the default. Reverting to the default value makes it 'clean' again.\n\nPersistent `dirty` state\n\n- **Libraries**: Angular Form, Vue FormKit.\n- **Behavior**: A field remains 'dirty' once changed, even if reverted to the default value.\n\nWe have chosen the persistent 'dirty' state model. To also support a non-persistent 'dirty' state, we introduce an additional flag:\n\n- _\"isDefaultValue\"_, whether the field's current value is the default value\n\n```ts\nconst { isDefaultValue, isTouched } = field.state.meta\n\n// The following line will re-create the non-Persistent `dirty` functionality.\nconst nonPersistentIsDirty = !isDefaultValue\n```\n\n![Field states extended](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/field-states-extended.png)\n\n## Field API\n\nThe Field API is an object accessed in the `tanstackField.api` property when creating a field. It provides methods for working with the field's state.\n\nExample:\n\n```angular-html\n<input\n  [value]=\"fieldName.api.state.value\"\n  (blur)=\"fieldName.api.handleBlur()\"\n  (input)=\"fieldName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n/>\n```\n\n## Validation\n\n`@tanstack/angular-form` provides both synchronous and asynchronous validation out of the box. Validation functions can be passed to the `tanstackField` directive using the `validators` prop.\n\nExample:\n\n```angular-ts\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"firstName\" #firstName=\"field\">\n      <input\n        [value]=\"firstName.api.state.value\"\n        (blur)=\"firstName.api.handleBlur()\"\n        (input)=\"firstName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n      />\n    </ng-container>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  firstNameValidator: FieldValidateFn<any, any, string, any> = ({ value }) =>\n    !value\n      ? 'A first name is required'\n      : value.length < 3\n        ? 'First name must be at least 3 characters'\n        : undefined\n\n  firstNameAsyncValidator: FieldValidateAsyncFn<any, string, any> = async ({\n    value,\n  }) => {\n    await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000))\n    return value.includes('error') && 'No \"error\" allowed in first name'\n  }\n\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\n## Validation with Standard Schema Libraries\n\nIn addition to hand-rolled validation options, we also support the [Standard Schema](https://github.com/standard-schema/standard-schema) specification.\n\nYou can define a schema using any of the libraries implementing the specification and pass it to a form or field validator.\n\nSupported libraries include:\n\n- [Zod](https://zod.dev/) (v3.24.0 or higher)\n- [Valibot](https://valibot.dev/) (v1.0.0 or higher)\n- [ArkType](https://arktype.io/) (v2.1.20 or higher)\n- [Yup](https://github.com/jquense/yup) (v1.7.0 or higher)\n\nExample:\n\n```angular-ts\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container\n      [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n      name=\"firstName\"\n      [validators]=\"{\n        onChange: z.string().min(3, 'First name must be at least 3 characters'),\n        onChangeAsyncDebounceMs: 500,\n        onChangeAsync: firstNameAsyncValidator,\n      }\"\n      #firstName=\"field\"\n    >\n      <!-- ... -->\n    </ng-container>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  firstNameAsyncValidator = z.string().refine(\n    async (value) => {\n      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000))\n      return !value.includes('error')\n    },\n    {\n      message: \"No 'error' allowed in first name\",\n    },\n  )\n\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  })\n\n  z = z\n}\n```\n\n## Reactivity\n\n`@tanstack/angular-form` offers a way to subscribe to form and field state changes via `injectStore(this.form, selector)`.\n\nExample:\n\n```typescript\nimport { injectForm, injectStore } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component(/*...*/)\nclass AppComponent {\n  form = injectForm(/*...*/)\n  canSubmit = injectStore(this.form, (state) => state.canSubmit)\n  isSubmitting = injectStore(this.form, (state) => state.isSubmitting)\n}\n```\n\n## Listeners\n\n`@tanstack/angular-form` allows you to react to specific triggers and \"listen\" to them to dispatch side effects.\n\nExample:\n\n```angular-ts\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container\n      [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n      name=\"country\"\n      [listeners]=\"{\n        onChange: onCountryChange\n      }\"\n      #country=\"field\"\n    ></ng-container>\n  `,\n})\n\n...\n\nonCountryChange: FieldListenerFn<any, any, any, any, string> = ({\n    value,\n  }) => {\n    console.log(`Country changed to: ${value}, resetting province`)\n    this.form.setFieldValue('province', '')\n  }\n```\n\nMore information can be found at [Listeners](./listeners.md)\n\n## Array Fields\n\nArray fields allow you to manage a list of values within a form, such as a list of hobbies. You can create an array field using the `tanstackField` directive.\n\nWhen working with array fields, you can use the fields `pushValue`, `removeValue`, `swapValues` and `moveValue` methods to add, remove, swap, and move a value from one index to another within the array, respectively. Additional helper methods such as `insertValue`, `replaceValue`, and `clearValues` are also available for inserting, replacing, and clearing array values.\n\nExample:\n\n```angular-ts\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [TanStackField],\n  template: `\n    <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"hobbies\" #hobbies=\"field\">\n      <div>\n        Hobbies\n        <div>\n          @if (!hobbies.api.state.value.length) {\n            No hobbies found\n          }\n          @for (_ of hobbies.api.state.value; track $index) {\n            <div>\n              <ng-container\n                [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n                [name]=\"getHobbyName($index)\"\n                #hobbyName=\"field\"\n              >\n                <div>\n                  <label [for]=\"hobbyName.api.name\">Name:</label>\n                  <input\n                    [id]=\"hobbyName.api.name\"\n                    [name]=\"hobbyName.api.name\"\n                    [value]=\"hobbyName.api.state.value\"\n                    (blur)=\"hobbyName.api.handleBlur()\"\n                    (input)=\"\n                      hobbyName.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\n                    \"\n                  />\n                  <button\n                    type=\"button\"\n                    (click)=\"hobbies.api.removeValue($index)\"\n                  >\n                    X\n                  </button>\n                </div>\n              </ng-container>\n              <ng-container\n                [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n                [name]=\"getHobbyDesc($index)\"\n                #hobbyDesc=\"field\"\n              >\n                <div>\n                  <label [for]=\"hobbyDesc.api.name\">Description:</label>\n                  <input\n                    [id]=\"hobbyDesc.api.name\"\n                    [name]=\"hobbyDesc.api.name\"\n                    [value]=\"hobbyDesc.api.state.value\"\n                    (blur)=\"hobbyDesc.api.handleBlur()\"\n                    (input)=\"\n                      hobbyDesc.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\n                    \"\n                  />\n                </div>\n              </ng-container>\n            </div>\n          }\n        </div>\n        <button type=\"button\" (click)=\"hobbies.api.pushValue(defaultHobby)\">\n          Add hobby\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    </ng-container>\n  `,\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  defaultHobby = {\n    name: '',\n    description: '',\n    yearsOfExperience: 0,\n  }\n\n  getHobbyName = (idx: number) => `hobbies[${idx}].name` as const\n  getHobbyDesc = (idx: number) => `hobbies[${idx}].description` as const\n\n  form = injectForm({\n    defaultValues: {\n      hobbies: [] as Array<{\n        name: string\n        description: string\n        yearsOfExperience: number\n      }>,\n    },\n    onSubmit({ value }) {\n      alert(JSON.stringify(value))\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\nThese are the basic concepts and terminology used in the `@tanstack/angular-form` library. Understanding these concepts will help you work more effectively with the library and create complex forms with ease.\n"}
